      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVII. Gif mon ungewintrædne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.28"/> wifmon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.29"/> to niedhæmde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.30"/> geðreatige, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.1"/> ðæt swa ðæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.2"/> gewintredan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.3"/> monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.star"/> bot.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.3-2"/> ungewintredne wifmon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.15"/> to nydhæmede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.4-2"/> geðreatige, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ðæt swa ðæs gewintredon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.2-2"/> monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.2-2"/> bot.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ungewintredes wifmannes slæge. Gyf man úng[e]wintredne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.1-4"/> wifman to nydhæmede g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>þreatige, sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> swa ðæs g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>wintredes mannes bot.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis uirginem immaturam ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.17"/> uiolentum concubitum perferendum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.1-3"/> cogat, sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_26.lnote.oe.2-3"/> hoc sicut adulte mulieris emendatio.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ungewintredes wifmannes slæge.] Gif mon ungewintrædne wifmon to niedhæmde geðreatige, sie ðæt swa ðæs gewintredan monnes<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Af_26.attnote.fn.15"/> bot.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="31" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="322" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXVII} Gif mon ungewintrædne wifmon to niedhæmde geðreatige, sie ðæt swa ðæs gewintredan monnes bot.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_26.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand ein unerwachsenes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_26.lnote.de.2"/> Mädchen zu Nothzucht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_26.lnote.de.3"/> drängt, sei das [so hoch zu büssen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_26.lnote.de.4"/>] wie die Busse für die erwachsene Person.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_26.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone forces an under-age girl to intercourse, let that be [compensated as highly] as the compensation for an adult person.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone rapes a girl who is not of age, the same compensation shall be paid to her as is paid to an adult.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="414" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone rapes a girl not of age, that is to be the same compensation as for an adult.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="323" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone rapes an underage girl, let the compensation be the same as for a mature person.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="270"><label>cites</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11-2">Af 11.2</ref> <quote>Note too that Af 18 (lewd approaches to nuns) and 26 (under-age rape) actually cite 11, 11:2 (equivalent for laity/adult)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11-2">Af 11.2–11.5</ref> <quote>26 (ref. 11:2–5)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_10">Abt 10–11</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_14">Abt 14</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_16">Abt 16</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_31">Abt 31</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_82">Abt 82–85</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="323"><label>shared vocabulary</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_38">Ine 38</ref> <quote>the term gewintred occurs in only one other place in West Saxon law: Ine §39</quote></note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">Whitelock numbers this chapter 26 and gives Liebermann’s number, 26, in brackets.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-redne <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-redne So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nyd. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> nydhæmede <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nyd. So; nydhæmede Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-des mennes <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-des mennes Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wifmonnes <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wifmonnes So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bót <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bót So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wif <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.;</hi> o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wif written above; o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_26.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
